<template>
    <heading>Controller</heading>
    <keywords>
        <li>controller</li>
        <li>event dispatch</li>
        <li>handler stack</li>
        <li>initialization</li>
        <li>state machine</li>
    </keywords>
    <section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p>Event dispatch is a kind of hierarchical state machine, implemented with a stack where push is a "call" and pop is a "return".</p>
        <p>Call <code>init(handler)</code> once to install the first handler. The stack is undefined until initialization creates it. An empty stack still records that initialization has occurred, so a second call throws an error even after dispatch removes the last handler.</p>
    </section>
    <section data-lp5-kind="code">
        <name>Outermost scope objects</name>
        <code><![CDATA[let controller = (() => {
    let handlerStack; // top of stack is current event handler

    function init(handler) {
        if (handlerStack !== undefined)
            throw new Error("Controller has already been initialized");
        handlerStack = [handler];
    }

    function baseEventHandler(event) {
        for (let handler; (handler = handlerStack.at(-1)) !== undefined; ) {
            let result = handler.dispatch.next(event);
            if (result.done)
                handlerStack.pop()
            else if (result.value === handler) // keep same handler
                return;
            else
                handlerStack.push(result.value);
        }
    }

    return {
        init: init,
        dispatch: baseEventHandler
    };
})();
]]></code>
    </section>
</template>
